  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "與世界連結：說故事的力量",
    "sub_ename": "THE STORY FACTOR：INSPIRATION, INFLUENCE AND PERSUASION THROUGH THE ART OF STORYTELLING",
    "describe_ch": "表達與演說是世界公民的基礎能力，而說故事永遠是發揮影響力的最佳方式，因為，誰不愛聽故事呢？\n這課程透過經典的案例分享，以傳記、短片等媒材，協助學生階段性的內在整理，看見之所以成為「現在的我」的家庭文化規條與社會發展脈絡，並將個人生命經驗成為結構化的故事。當能夠說好、書寫自己的故事，也就讓自己真實在人間「現身」。同時結合聆聽練習與回饋機制，當每個人能好好聽完別人的故事，體會他人的內在動機及成長軌跡，就有可能開展新的眼光，開啟尊重多元價值的健康心態。\n最終，共同研讀聯合國永續發展目標SDGs，選擇一個與自己有關的議題，說出一個能夠發揮影響力的故事，屬於自己/家族/地方/國族/世界的故事。\n",
    "describe_eh": "For global citizens, expression and presentation are the fundamental skills and storytelling is always the best way to extend the messages students would like to pass over; who would reject stories?\nThrough classic case studies from biographies and short films, this lesson will assist students to organize their mindsets, understand why they became who they are from the family, society as well as personal perspectives. Via this lecture, students will be able to fully tell their life stories and experience to peers, recognize and appreciate the others’ stories, and exchange and feel different viewpoints.\nThis lecture will review the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), and allow students to choose one of topics related to their issues and experiences, and tell their very own story in front of the class.\n",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "研讀經典案例並整合個人經驗，以具備清楚表達的能力及溝通交流的勇氣，同時啟蒙學生跨域學習潛能。",
      "describe_en": "Case study by structuring personal experience and knowledge to extend and expand their communication ability in multiple ways."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "連結聯合國永續發展目標SDGs，開展自己的內在關懷，並思考當今影響人類未來發展之核心課題。",
      "describe_en": "Combine the principle of the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), to develop the inner kindness and thoughtfulness, and study the current society impact and future potential issues."
    }
  ],
